/target
**/*.rs.bk
.DS_Store
/parity-logs

# nix build output symlink
result
result-*
.overnight/
data/
# …except the card data VENDORED into a crate, which is source: the kernel
# must not read outside the workspace, so NSG's canonical subtype list is
# checked in and `include_str!`d. Without this the crate does not build.
!/crates/jinteki-cr/data/
# …and NSG's format/card-pool data, vendored for the same reason: the format
# guard (crates/jinteki-server/tests/formats.rs) computes each deck's card
# pool from it, and must not reach outside the workspace to do so.
!/crates/jinteki-server/data/
